      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HALF HOLIDAY (2) led and faded to midfield when tackling a higher-graded race last start. Had won his other two starts of this campaign, both coming at this circuit and distance. He has the speed to take advantage of a low draw and will enjoy the class drop. KAIRAKI DELIGHT NZ (1) ended last prep with a sixth at Menangle 11 weeks ago but is a two-time fresh winner who has been readied with a trial. Aided by the ace draw so is capable of a strong return. PENURIOUS (3) is hard to knock having come from this barrier to win his last two outings, one at this circuit and distance and the other at Menangle. Up in grade but could register the hat-trick. VINCENTIUS MAXIMUS (4) has been solid from wider barriers in his two starts off a spell and should be close to peak fitness.",
